# FDD 05 — System Administration - Credentialing (Feature 5.1-5.6) review.
#
# Source: "5 - System Admin - Credentialing.docx" (functional-design-docs/05 - System
# Administration - Credentialing/). Header: "This document details the requirement for a
# System Administrator - Credentialing to manage master data such as Certificate/Permit
# types, Endorsements, Global parameters, Run & view Batch jobs, worklist assignments and
# Reports." This FDD is the PRIMARY source for two open questions already flagged in
# credentialing-technical-design.ttl from the Phase 1 pass: Question_ConfigurabilityModel
# (Feature 5.3, "Global Parameters"/"Credentialing Controls") and
# Question_BatchJobAdminVisibility (Feature 5.4, "Run & View Batch Jobs"). Both are
# updated below with new evidence from this FDD rather than duplicated — see the
# Cross-cutting Annotations section, which asserts additional triples directly onto
# those existing subject IRIs (RDF triples merge across files; this is the intended
# "update the existing Annotation" mechanism per fdd-review/CONVENTIONS.md).
#
# Structure of the source document itself (relevant to how this ingestion is organized):
# - The "Business Specifications" narrative section describes MORE ground than the
#   "Addendum" section's numbered user stories cover. The Addendum only formalizes
#   Features 5.1-5.4 in full (5.1.1-5.1.7 ish, 5.2.1-5.2.9, 5.3.1-5.3.5, 5.4.1-5.4.4);
#   Feature 5.5 (Manage Worklist Assignment) is an unfinished stub in the Addendum
#   (literally "5.5. / Acceptance Criteria / T" and a second truncated story) even
#   though the narrative section describes it in full detail with three wireframes
#   (11/12/13); Feature 5.6 (Reports) is a pure deferral pointer to Feature 2.1.
#   The narrative section ALSO describes several further admin capabilities (Alternative
#   Test Scores, Online Credentialing Viewing for out-of-state EPPs, Public Credential
#   Search page administration, Credential system pages administration, Alerts/
#   Notifications management, Email template management, Document upload management,
#   file-queue/API-data-ingestion administration, Question Sets management, Internal
#   Comments management) that were NEVER split into their own Addendum user stories at
#   all — the FDD's own header scopes it to "5.1-5.6" but the narrative content runs
#   well past what got formalized. Per fdd-review/CONVENTIONS.md's instruction to use
#   the FDD's own numbered-user-story granularity as the Requirement unit (not invent
#   numbering the source never gave), these un-formalized narrative-only items are NOT
#   modeled as individual sd:Requirement nodes here — most of them explicitly defer to
#   other Business Specifications the narrative names directly (Alerts/Emails -> Epic
#   6.0/Communications, Reports -> Feature 2.1/Reporting, Document upload -> Documents
#   capability, Public Search page -> Business Specs 31.1/31.2), so they are out-of-scope
#   for Credentialing rather than gaps in it. This is noted collectively in
#   Annotation_UnformalizedAdminNarrativeContent below rather than forced into fake
#   "5.7"/"5.8" Requirement numbers the FDD itself never assigned.
# - "HIGH LEVEL SCENARIOS" table (Ref 1-42): skipped per convention — paraphrases the
#   same Business Specifications content at coarser granularity, no added traceability.
# - Comments (word/comments.xml + commentsExtensible.xml): 41 total across two comment
#   systems — an older thread (Caswell/DTMB-Contractor, Dontje/MDE, Groom/CEPI, dated
#   2025-07 through 2026-04-15) and a newer batch of large-integer-ID comments (Doherty/
#   MDE-Contractor relaying "Yashi", dated 2026-04-21) that read as the FINAL round of
#   resolution on this document. Most are single-word acknowledgements ("Noted",
#   "Clarified", "Needs discussion") not worth individually modeling; the substantive
#   ones are used below. Two are load-bearing for cross-domain findings: comment #128
#   (Dontje, "we don't want to have users assigned specific/custom access; it needs to
#   remain role-based") and its resolution (comment 203926376, Doherty/Yashi: "I have
#   completely revised this user story... search for User Roles... and manage the
#   worklist and report assignments globally for that role") directly contradict the
#   FDD's own narrative-section prose and Wireframes 11-13, which describe and show
#   individual-level assignment — see Annotation_WorklistAssignmentRoleVsIndividual.
# - Tracked changes: not reconstructed as a diff; where a comment thread shows the
#   visible text is stale relative to a later decision (worklist assignment, above;
#   the "Type"->"Credential Type" column rename per comment 2044568528), that's called
#   out in the relevant Requirement's sd:notes rather than treated as settled.
# - Wireframes: TWO distinct generations of imagery exist in this docx. image1.png -
#   image13.png are legacy MOECS-styled screens that map cleanly, in document order, to
#   the narrative section's "Wireframe 1" through "Wireframe 13" captions (images
#   precede their caption in this doc, confirmed by direct viewing of images 1, 7, 9, 11
#   against their captions) — all 13 extracted below. image14.png-image28.png (15
#   further images) are a SECOND, later, MiEdWorkforce-branded redesign with no adjacent
#   captions at all, appearing only in the Addendum's vicinity; confirmed by viewing
#   image14 (a "Certificates" list page matching Addendum story 5.1.1 almost exactly —
#   Search field, Add Certificate action, filter/download actions), image20 (an "Add
#   Endorsement" Requirements tab showing Grade Levels/Codes and Test Codes tables,
#   matching 5.2.6/5.2.8/5.2.9), and image28 (a public "Educator Credential Search"
#   page, corroborating cred:Op_SearchPublicEducatorCredentials). Only these 3 of the 15
#   redesign images were individually viewed — same "confirm the general shape, don't
#   hand-catalogue all of them" approach the FDD 11/16 pilot used for its own image
#   cluster; the remaining 12 are presumed to be further redesign screens for
#   5.2-5.5 not individually reviewed here.

@prefix sd:    <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:> .
@prefix oa:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix cred:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:credentialing:> .
@prefix iam:   <urn:solutiondesign:instance:iam:> .

