#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 5.1: Managing Certificate/Permit Types
#################################################################

cred:Req_05_1_1 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.1.1" ;
    sd:title "View a searchable list of certificate/permit types" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want to view a list of types, so that I can review and manage core credential definitions within the system." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Page accessible from the Credentialing Data area. Searchable, tabular list of certificate types (Name, Status). Search field filters by name. 'Add Certificate' action initiates creation of a new certificate type. Filter and download actions refine/export the list. Only certificate types configured in the system are displayed." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_ListCredentialDefinitions ;
    sd:notes "Good match for the list/search/create core; cred:Op_CreateCredentialDefinition covers 'Add Certificate'. Filter/download-as-export actions shown in Wireframe05_14_Redesign have no corresponding sd:parameters/export-format detail on cred:Op_ListCredentialDefinitions — same minor, low-impact UI-export gap the FDD 11/16 pilot flagged for worklist search (Question_MissingWorklistSearchAndExportUX), not re-raised as its own Annotation here." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

cred:Req_05_1_2 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.1.2" ;
    sd:title "View Type/Modified By/Modified On in search results" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want to view details including Type, Modified By, and Modified On in the search results table, so that I can see audit information at a glance." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Results table populated per selected category with Type/Modified By/Modified On columns; user selects a row to open the detailed record." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_ListCredentialDefinitions ;
    sd:notes "Per comment 2044568528 ('It has been updated to Credential Type'), the 'Type' column itself was renamed to 'Credential Type' late in review — the acceptance criteria text above is the pre-rename wording. Modified By/Modified On are not explicit fields on cred:CredentialDefinitionVersion in credentialing-domain.ttl today (that entity's own description is generic 'audit trail' prose) — minor gap, folded into Req_05_1_4's note rather than duplicated." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

cred:Req_05_1_3 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.1.3" ;
    sd:title "Edit a Type's Validity, Fee, and Effective From fields" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want to edit a Type and update fields like Validity, Fee, and Effective From date, so that I can maintain current credential requirements." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Selecting a Certificate Type opens a detailed, editable view: Category Name, Type, Print Name, Is Permanent?, Is Advanced?, Is Active?, Validity (years), Fee, Effective From date. Effective From captures when the changes become active." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_UpdateCredentialDefinition, cred:CredentialProperties, cred:CredentialDefinitionFeeSchedule, cred:CredentialDefinitionValidityPeriod, cred:CredentialDefinitionEffectiveDateRange ;
    sd:notes "Strong direct match — CredentialProperties already carries IsPermanent/IsAdvanced/IsActive/CanApply/CanRenew, and FeeSchedule/ValidityPeriod/EffectiveDateRange cover the rest. Comment #9/#10 (Caswell -> Dontje, 'Yes it should be editable') confirms future-dated Effective From edits are intentional, not an oversight — this is the admin-facing origin of cred:BatchJob_DefinitionVersionActivation (the nightly 'Cleanup of Future-Dated Changes' job in credentialing-technical-design.ttl), which activates exactly these future-dated changes. See Req_05_1_5 for the versioning-on-save behavior this feeds." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

cred:Req_05_1_4 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.1.4" ;
    sd:title "Capture Modified By/Modified On audit details on save" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want the system to capture Modified By and Modified On details upon saving changes, so that I have an audit trail of modifications." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "System captures the identity of the user making changes (Modified By) and the timestamp (Modified On) upon save; both visible in the search results table for the modified record." ;
    sd:notes "No satisfiedBy: cred:CredentialDefinitionVersion (credentialing-domain.ttl) is described only as generically carrying 'change audit trail' with no explicit Modified By/Modified On fields listed in sd:fields anywhere on CredentialDefinitionAggregate's entities/value objects. Comment #78 (Dontje, 'Further discussion about audit details/history is needed') shows this was still an open point on the client side too, not just a modeling gap on our end. Genuine coverage gap." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

cred:Req_05_1_5 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.1.5" ;
    sd:title "Version the record based on Effective From date upon save" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want the system to version the record based on the Effective From date upon save, so that changes are applied correctly to new applications." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "On save, system versions the certificate record based on Effective From; current date is the default Effective From; changes affect only new applications generated after the effective date, existing/pending applications unaffected." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Rule_CredentialDefinitionVersioning, cred:CredentialDefinitionEffectiveDateRange, cred:BatchJob_DefinitionVersionActivation ;
    sd:notes "Direct, well-corroborated match — this is precisely what Rule_CredentialDefinitionVersioning plus BatchJob_DefinitionVersionActivation (the nightly job that actually flips a future-dated version to Active once its Effective From date arrives) already model. This FDD story is the missing admin-UI-side confirmation that the batch job's premise (admins schedule changes in advance) is real product behavior, not a speculative technical-design assumption." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

cred:Req_05_1_6 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.1.6" ;
    sd:title "Edit Permit-specific fields (Can Apply/Can Renew/rich-text Message)" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want to edit permit-specific fields, so that I can maintain the distinct configuration permits require beyond what certificates need." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Selecting a Permit type opens a detailed view with editable Category Name, Type, Print Name, Is Permanent?, Is Advanced?, Is Active?, Can Apply?, Can Renew?, Fee, Effective From, plus a 'Message' field with Rich Text Editor formatting." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:CredentialProperties, cred:Op_UpdateCredentialDefinition ;
    sd:notes "CanApply/CanRenew are already modeled on CredentialProperties. Genuine small gap: no rich-text 'Message' field exists anywhere on CredentialDefinitionAggregate's value objects. Comment #32/#33 (Caswell: 'Can a permit be permanent?' / Dontje: 'There are legacy permits that are permanent') doesn't conflict with the existing invariant ('If IsPermanent=true then CanRenew must=false') since that invariant is already generic across credential types, not certificate-only — no change needed, just confirmation permits use the same flag. Per comment 1332550677 ('Thank you. We can remove this user story'), a draft bullet proposing admins could 'optionally add internal comments about the update' on this screen was agreed to be removed during review — not carried into the acceptance criteria above, and not counted as a separate gap." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

cred:Req_05_1_7 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.1.7" ;
    sd:title "Rename the 'Type' (name) field of an existing record" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want the ability to change the 'Type' (name) field of an existing record, so that I can update the credential name to reflect current administrative naming conventions." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "The 'Type' field (functioning as the record's name) is editable within the record details screen; admins can rename an existing type; the change is saved and versioned per the standard save logic." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_UpdateCredentialDefinition, cred:Rule_CredentialDefinitionVersioning ;
    sd:notes "This is the FDD's own unnumbered addendum story (rendered '5.1.' in the source with no digit — an evident drafting gap, assigned 5.1.7 here for a stable IRI). Straightforward extension of the same update+versioning path as 5.1.3/5.1.5." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 5.2: Managing Endorsements (CIP Codes included)
#################################################################

cred:Req_05_2_1 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.2.1" ;
    sd:title "Manage Endorsement Classifications (create/edit endorsements)" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want to manage Endorsement Classifications so that I can maintain the organization of credential categories." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "List of existing classifications (Code/Name/Certificate Type/Subject Area/Modified By/Modified Date/Is Active). 'Create Endorsement' requires Endorsement Name, Certificate Type, Subject Area, Status, with Core/Grade-band-not-applicable checkboxes under Subject Area. 'Edit' updates Endorsement Name/Certificate Type/Subject Area/Status. Within an endorsement, admins manage Grade Levels/Codes (Grade Band/Code/Out-of-State/Start/End Date) and Test Codes (Grade Band/Code/All Tests Required/Test Start/End Date), and select applicable Certificates/Temporary Credentials." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_CreateEndorsementDefinition, cred:Op_UpdateEndorsementDefinition, cred:EndorsementDefinitionAggregate ;
    sd:notes "Good match. The FDD's own terminology is loose here — the narrative section separately describes a 'Manage Endorsement Classification' page (Class Name/Class Description/Is Active) distinct from full endorsement management, but this Addendum story conflates 'Endorsement Classification' with creating/editing a full Endorsement — treated as one requirement against EndorsementDefinitionAggregate, consistent with how the underlying domain model doesn't separately break out a 'classification' sub-concept either." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

cred:Req_05_2_2 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.2.2" ;
    sd:title "Search existing endorsements" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want to search for existing endorsements, so that I can quickly locate records for management." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Search filters: CIP Code, Name, Cert Type, Subject Area, Modified By, Modified Date, Status, Include Inactive Endorsements, Begin/End Date, Progress to Professional, Out-of-State applicants, Initial endorsement eligible?" ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_ListEndorsementDefinitions ;
    sd:notes "Operation exists as a generic list; the specific filter fields (CIP Code, Progress to Professional, Out-of-State, Initial-endorsement-eligible) are not individually modeled as sd:parameters on cred:Op_ListEndorsementDefinitions — consistent with the ontology's guidance that filter parameters stay opaque prose rather than a promoted class; not counted as a separate gap." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

cred:Req_05_2_3 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.2.3" ;
    sd:title "Restrict the Cert Type filter to Teacher and School Administrator" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want the Cert Type filter to only display Teacher and School Administrator options, since endorsements are only available for those types." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "The 'Cert Type' dropdown filter on the Endorsement search page contains only 'Teacher' and 'School Administrator'; other credential types do not appear." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_ListEndorsementDefinitions ;
    sd:notes "Pure UI filter-option restriction; no corresponding invariant exists on CredentialCategory/EndorsementDefinitionAggregate limiting which categories can carry endorsements, though it's consistent with the domain model's own description ('subject area specializations added to teaching certificates'). Low-impact, not raised as a separate Annotation." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

cred:Req_05_2_4 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.2.4" ;
    sd:title "View Code/Name/Certificate Type/Subject Area/Modified By/Modified Date in search results" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want to view search results including Code, Name, Certificate Type, Subject Area, Modified By, and Modified Date, so that I can track recent changes." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Results table with Code/Name/Certificate Type/Subject Area/Modified By/Modified Date columns; clicking a record opens it for editing." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_ListEndorsementDefinitions ;
    sd:notes "Same Modified By/Modified Date audit-field gap noted on Req_05_1_4 applies here too — EndorsementDefinitionVersion has no explicit audit fields listed either." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

cred:Req_05_2_5 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.2.5" ;
    sd:title "Reset endorsement search filters" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want a Reset option on the endorsement search page, so that I can quickly clear entered criteria and restore defaults." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "A Reset action clears all entered search criteria and reverts dropdowns/checkboxes to defaults." ;
    sd:notes "No satisfiedBy: pure client-side UX affordance with no domain-model or API counterpart expected — consistent with how the FDD 11/16 pilot treated equivalent Reset-button stories as not worth a coverage-gap Annotation on their own (too low-impact to be the 'point' of the exercise). Not modeled as a gap." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

cred:Req_05_2_6 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.2.6" ;
    sd:title "Manage endorsement codes (Add/Edit/Delete) in a table" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want to manage endorsement codes in a table format, allowing me to Add, Edit (dates/fields), and Delete rows, so that I can define specific validity parameters." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Endorsement Code table supports Add/Edit(Begin/End Date, etc.)/Delete." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:Op_UpdateEndorsementDefinition, cred:GradeBandRange ;
    sd:notes "Per comment 156325117 (Doherty relaying Yashi, 2026-04-21): 'Delete' was refined late in review to apply ONLY to endorsement codes that have never been active/utilized — a code that has been active cannot be deleted, only 'retired' by setting an End Date. This is a real, specific business rule (a delete-guard tied to activation history) not currently expressed anywhere in credentialing-domain.ttl's invariants for EndorsementDefinitionAggregate; folded into this Requirement's notes rather than minted as its own sd:BusinessRule given its narrow scope, but worth carrying forward if EndorsementCode/GradeBandRange ever gets its own dedicated lifecycle." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

cred:Req_05_2_7 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.2.7" ;
    sd:title "Notify System Admin to define assignment mappings when a new endorsement code is added" ;
    sd:statement "As the MiEdWorkforce system, when a new endorsement code is added, I want to generate a notification/task for the MiEdWorkforce System Admin, so that allowable assignment mappings are defined." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Saving a new Endorsement Code automatically triggers a notification/task routed to the MiEdWorkforce System Admin, alerting them to define the allowable assignment mappings for appropriate placement of the new endorsement." ;
    sd:notes "No satisfiedBy: cred:EndorsementDefinitionUpdatedEvent is the closest existing event (adding a code is an update to the EndorsementDefinition) but no notification/task-routing behavior is modeled off it, and 'allowable assignment mappings for Appropriate Placement' is itself a Staffing-domain concept per this FDD's own Dependencies section ('credential data... available for mapping to assignments — Managing Credential use of Assignment Codes 12.1'), a business specification not yet converted anywhere in mied-v3. Genuine, cross-domain coverage gap — the notification mechanism belongs to Credentialing (on EndorsementDefinitionUpdatedEvent) but the mapping being defined belongs to a domain this project hasn't reached yet." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

cred:Req_05_2_8 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.2.8" ;
    sd:title "Define MTTC test-code requirements via comma-separated codes" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want to define MTTC requirements in the Test Code table using comma-separated test codes, so that multiple required tests can be mapped to an endorsement." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Test Codes table: Grade Band, Code, Test Codes (comma-separated), All Tests Required, Test Start/End Dates, Certificates, Temporary Credentials (comma-separated)." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:RequiredAssessments ;
    sd:notes "Good conceptual match — RequiredAssessments already models AssessmentIdentifier/CombinationLogic/MinimumScore per endorsement. The FDD's comma-separated-text input shape is a UI/data-entry detail, not a structural gap." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

cred:Req_05_2_9 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.2.9" ;
    sd:title "Toggle All-Tests-Required vs. any-single-test-passes logic" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want the option to designate whether All Test Codes Required must be passed, or if passing just one is sufficient for the endorsement." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "'All Tests Required' column: Yes requires every listed test code to pass; No requires only one of the listed test codes to pass." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:RequiredAssessments ;
    sd:notes "Direct match — this is exactly RequiredAssessments.CombinationLogic (AND/OR), also confirmed as the 'All Tests Required' flag by cred:Rule_SubjectAreaAssessmentValidation's own existing notes (per the FDD 11/16 pilot's Req_11_8_1)." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 5.3: Managing Global Parameters
#################################################################

cred:Req_05_3_1 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.3.1" ;
    sd:title "Search Credentialing Controls by Parameter Description" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want to search for Credentialing Controls by Parameter Description, so that I can quickly find the parameter I need to update." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "A 'Manage Credentialing Controls' page with a 'Parameter Description' search field and a Search button." ;
    sd:notes "No satisfiedBy — see Annotation_ConfigurabilityModelEvidence below (updates cred:Question_ConfigurabilityModel)." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

cred:Req_05_3_2 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.3.2" ;
    sd:title "View Description/Value/Format/audit details in Credentialing Controls results" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want to view the Description, Value, Format, and audit details (Modified By, Modified On) in the search results table, so that I understand the control's configuration and history." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Results table: Description, Value, Format, Modified By, Modified On." ;
    sd:notes "No satisfiedBy — see Annotation_ConfigurabilityModelEvidence." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

cred:Req_05_3_3 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.3.3" ;
    sd:title "Update a Credentialing Control's Description" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want to update the Description of a Credentialing Control, so that I can clarify its purpose within the system." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Description field is editable within the record details view and savable." ;
    sd:notes "No satisfiedBy — see Annotation_ConfigurabilityModelEvidence." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

cred:Req_05_3_4 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.3.4" ;
    sd:title "Update a Credentialing Control's Value" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want to update the Value of a Credentialing Control, so that I can change associated system text or configurations (e.g. credentialing landing page text or specific fee amounts)." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Value field accepts text or configuration values for credentialing-specific messaging or parameters; editable and savable." ;
    sd:notes "No satisfiedBy — see Annotation_ConfigurabilityModelEvidence. Note the FDD's own example pairs a free-text landing-page-message use case with a numeric fee-amount use case in the SAME flat Value field — direct textual evidence for option (c) ('fully centralized, no per-type variation') in Question_ConfigurabilityModel's three competing shapes, though it doesn't settle the cross-domain-ownership half of that question." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

cred:Req_05_3_5 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.3.5" ;
    sd:title "Capture Modified By/Modified On on Credentialing Control save" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want the system to capture Modified By and Modified On audit details when saving changes to the control, so that I can maintain an audit trail of modifications to credentialing configurations." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "On Save, system captures user identity (Modified By) and timestamp (Modified On), immediately reflected in the results table." ;
    sd:notes "No satisfiedBy — see Annotation_ConfigurabilityModelEvidence." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 5.4: Run & View Batch Jobs
#################################################################

cred:Req_05_4_1 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.4.1" ;
    sd:title "Search batch job status by Run Date and Batch Job name" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want to search for batch job status using filters like Run Date and Batch Job name, so that I can monitor specific job history." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Page for managing/viewing batch jobs; filters for Run Date and Batch Job (dropdown of available job names); Search button." ;
    sd:notes "No satisfiedBy — see Annotation_BatchJobAdminVisibilityEvidence below (updates cred:Question_BatchJobAdminVisibility)." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

cred:Req_05_4_2 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.4.2" ;
    sd:title "View batch job run history table" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want to view the Batch job table including Run Status, Run Start/End Dates, and an auto-generated Run Status Description, so that I can easily assess the outcome and duration of past job executions." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Results table: Batch Job, Run Status, Run Start Date (date+time), Run End Date (date+time), auto-generated Run Status Description." ;
    sd:notes "No satisfiedBy — see Annotation_BatchJobAdminVisibilityEvidence. Wireframe05_9 (confirmed by viewing) shows exactly this table, already populated with real run history and free-text status descriptions (e.g. 'File(s) Processed: MDEEducatorLicense_250417.txt (Total 6): processed (0))', 'No records to update')." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

cred:Req_05_4_3 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.4.3" ;
    sd:title "Manually execute a predefined batch job" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want to manually execute a predefined batch job from a list, so that I can run required jobs on demand." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Admin selects a batch job from a predefined, fixed list and triggers immediate manual execution; the admin cannot add new batch job types to the list." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy cred:BatchJob_DefinitionVersionActivation, cred:BatchJob_CredentialExpirationProcessing ;
    sd:notes "Partial: satisfiedBy points at the two batch jobs this manual-execution capability WOULD apply to if the admin console existed, per credentialing-technical-design.ttl — but no ApiOperation/Sequence models the manual-trigger console itself anywhere in the graph. See Annotation_BatchJobAdminVisibilityEvidence: comment #127 (Dontje, on the Feature 5.4 heading itself) shows the client was still actively discussing whether re-run-on-demand should even be allowed and what authorization it needs, as of the last comment on that thread — i.e. even the source FDD hadn't settled this by the time of ingestion." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

cred:Req_05_4_4 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.4.4" ;
    sd:title "Capture audit details for manual batch job execution" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want the system to capture audit details when I manually execute a batch job, so that there is a record of the manual intervention." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "On manual execution, system records the initiating user's identity and the timestamp of the manual run." ;
    sd:notes "No satisfiedBy — see Annotation_BatchJobAdminVisibilityEvidence. Comment #128 (Dontje, anchored to this same acceptance-criteria text) is actually about Feature 5.5's role-vs-individual question, not this story — an apparent comment-anchor drift in the source docx; not treated as bearing on this Requirement." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 5.5: Manage Worklist Assignment (Addendum stub)
#################################################################

cred:Req_05_5_1 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.5.1" ;
    sd:title "Assign worklist and/or report access to a user or role" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want to assign worklist and/or report access, so that the right staff can see the applications and reports relevant to their job." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "The Addendum's own text for this story is a stub ('5.5. / Acceptance Criteria / T') — reconstructed here from the narrative Business Specifications section instead: admin searches by User Type (EPP/School District/Applicant, each with type-specific extra filters), selects a user from results, and manages that user's Worklist assignment (list of worklists) and Report access assignment (list of reports), with audit capture (Modified By/On) on updates." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy iam:RoleDefinitionAggregate ;
    sd:notes "PARTIAL and CONTRADICTED match — see Annotation_WorklistAssignmentRoleVsIndividual below. The narrative text and Wireframes 11-13 (all confirmed by viewing) describe and show INDIVIDUAL-level assignment (searching for and editing a specific named person's worklist/report access), directly matching what credentialing-domain.ttl's own Question_WorklistAssignmentScope already anticipated from the FDD 11/16 pass. But the FINAL review comment on this FDD (203926376, Doherty relaying Yashi, 2026-04-21) reverses this: 'Since worklist and report management is strictly role-based and not assigned at the individual user level, I have completely revised this user story... search for User Roles (filtered by User Type) and manage the worklist and report assignments globally for that role' — directly responding to comment #128 (Dontje: 'We don't want to have users assigned specific/custom access; it needs to remain role-based'). iam:RoleDefinitionAggregate is the correct home for the FINAL (role-based) shape, but it currently has no exposed manage/update API (iam-api.ttl only has read-only Op_ListRoles/Op_GetRole) and no first-class 'worklist' or 'report' concept as an assignable unit distinct from an ordinary Permission — so even the settled version of this requirement is not actually modeled end-to-end anywhere yet." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

cred:Req_05_5_2 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.5.2" ;
    sd:title "View a user's/role's assigned report access" ;
    sd:statement "As a Credential Admin, I want to view a user's assigned Report access, so that I can verify which reports they are authorized to run." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Also an Addendum stub (title text present, Acceptance Criteria section left empty). Reconstructed from Wireframe05_13 (confirmed by viewing): a 'Manage Report assignment' screen listing reports currently assigned." ;
    sd:notes "Same contradiction and gap as Req_05_5_1 — see Annotation_WorklistAssignmentRoleVsIndividual. cred:Perm_ReportsView (Cat_Reporting) is the closest existing permission concept but models scope-based report visibility, not an assignable per-user/per-role list of specific named reports." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

#################################################################
# Requirement — Feature 5.6: Reports (feature-level pointer)
#################################################################

cred:Req_05_6 a sd:Requirement ;
    sd:requirementId "5.6" ;
    sd:title "Reports (feature-level pointer)" ;
    sd:statement "The reporting capabilities described for this feature align with the broader reporting functionality defined under Feature 2.1. As outlined in those user stories, administrators (scoped by functional area) are expected to have access to the same reporting capabilities." ;
    sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "out-of-scope" ;
    rdfs:comment "Feature 5.6 explicitly defers all reporting/report-administration behavior to Feature 2.1 (Reporting), not modeled by Credentialing. The narrative section's own reports-management content (retiring report availability, role-based report access, ad-hoc/custom report creation, export options, report-resource text management) is the same deferred content — not modeled as its own Requirement per this file's header note on unformalized narrative content." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_05_6 ; sd:status "resolved" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

#################################################################
# Cross-cutting Annotations — updates to credentialing's existing open questions
#
# These assert additional triples directly onto the SAME subject IRIs already declared
# in credentialing-technical-design.ttl (Phase 1) and credentialing-domain.ttl, per
# fdd-review/CONVENTIONS.md's instruction to update/cross-reference rather than
# duplicate. RDF triples merge across files at load time; this is not a redeclaration.
#################################################################

cred:Question_ConfigurabilityModel
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_05_3_1, cred:Req_05_3_2, cred:Req_05_3_3, cred:Req_05_3_4, cred:Req_05_3_5 ;
    sd:resolutionNotes "FDD 05 Feature 5.3 (this file's primary source for this question) does NOT resolve which of the three competing configurability shapes was chosen — it neither confirms nor rules out per-credential-type variation in so many words. But it supplies concrete new evidence leaning toward shape (c), 'fully centralized, no per-type variation': Wireframe05_7 (confirmed by viewing) shows a single FLAT 'Credentialing Controls' results table with genuinely heterogeneous, unrelated example rows (a numeric fee-like value, a free-text 'Governor'/'Charter' pair, a datetime-format string) and no credential-type-scoping column anywhere in the search filters (only 'Parameter Description') or results columns (Description/Value/Format/Modified By/Modified On). This reads as a generic system-wide key-value settings store, not a per-credential-type override mechanism — more centralized than even shape (c) originally envisioned (which still assumed some per-type structure), closer to a flat global settings table that happens to include credentialing-relevant entries among unrelated ones (e.g. 'Governor'/'Charter' looks unrelated to credentialing at all). This actually strengthens the OTHER half of the open question — whether 'Global Parameters' is even credentialing-owned rather than a shared cross-domain configuration capability — since the sample data shown isn't credentialing-specific. Still open; not resolved by this FDD." ;
    sd:status "open" .

cred:Question_BatchJobAdminVisibility
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_05_4_1, cred:Req_05_4_2, cred:Req_05_4_3, cred:Req_05_4_4 ;
    sd:resolutionNotes "FDD 05 Feature 5.4 (this file's primary source for this question) resolves the FIRST half affirmatively: yes, batch jobs are meant to be admin-visible and searchable/executable through a generic 'Run & View Batch Jobs' console, not purely internal scheduled logic — Wireframe05_9 (confirmed by viewing) shows this console already exists as real/legacy functionality, populated with 8+ real job names, run history, and free-text status descriptions. None of those job names literally match cred:BatchJob_DefinitionVersionActivation or cred:BatchJob_CredentialExpirationProcessing (closest conceptual overlaps: 'Process Credential data (Daily)' and 'Delete Certificate Applications (Daily)' x3), so whether OUR two specific batch jobs are meant to surface through this exact console, or are distinct nightly processes alongside it, remains unconfirmed. The SECOND half (exact nightly run time, generic-console-as-credentialing-owned-vs-platform-tooling) stays open, and a NEW open point surfaces: comment #127 (Dontje, anchored to the Feature 5.4 heading) shows the client was still actively discussing, as of the last comment on that thread, whether jobs should support 1) a 'health report' and/or 2) re-run-on-demand with what authorization implications — i.e. even the source FDD's own review process hadn't settled the manual re-run/authorization question by ingestion time. Impact downgraded from the admin-visibility question (now largely answered) to this narrower re-run/authorization sub-question." ;
    sd:status "open" .

cred:Question_WorklistAssignmentScope
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_05_5_1, cred:Req_05_5_2, iam:RoleDefinitionAggregate ;
    sd:resolutionNotes "UPDATE from the actual FDD 05 review (the prior cross-reference to 'fdd-sdd-review/reviews/05-system-admin-credentialing.md, Coverage Gap #4' predates this ingestion and reflects only the FDD's stale narrative text/wireframes, not its final resolution). This FDD's own review comments reverse the individual-assignment premise: comment #128 (Dontje, MDE) states 'We don't want to have users assigned specific/custom access; it needs to remain role-based while still allowing the admin to update those attributes for the role', and the FDD's final comment on the matching user story (203926376, Doherty relaying Yashi, 2026-04-21) confirms 'Since worklist and report management is strictly role-based and not assigned at the individual user level, I have completely revised this user story... search for User Roles (filtered by User Type) and manage the worklist and report assignments globally for that role.' So the premise this Annotation was originally raised against (individual-level worklist assignment as real product behavior) is the OPPOSITE of the client's final decision — worklist/report access assignment is role-based, via iam:RoleDefinitionAggregate, not a per-individual queue-assignment concept. This doesn't fully close the question, though: iam:RoleDefinitionAggregate has no exposed manage/update API today (iam-api.ttl's only Role operations are read-only Op_ListRoles/Op_GetRole), and neither 'worklist' nor 'report' exists anywhere as a first-class, nameable, assignable unit distinct from an ordinary Permission — so the SETTLED (role-based) version of this capability is arguably a bigger, still-unmodeled gap than the individual-assignment version this Annotation originally described." ;
    sd:status "open" .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "coverage-gap" ;
    rdfs:comment "No explicit Modified By/Modified On fields exist on cred:CredentialDefinitionVersion or cred:EndorsementDefinitionVersion (credentialing-domain.ttl) despite both this FDD's Certificate/Permit-type stories (5.1.2, 5.1.4) and its Endorsement stories (5.2.4) requiring them to be captured and displayed. Comment #78 (Dontje, MDE) shows 'further discussion about audit details/history is needed' was still open on the client side too, not just a modeling gap on our end." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_05_1_4, cred:Req_05_2_4 ;
    sd:impact "L" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "coverage-gap" ;
    rdfs:comment "No Reset-filters affordance is modeled anywhere for Endorsement search, consistent with how the FDD 11/16 pilot treated equivalent Reset-button stories elsewhere in the graph — a pure client-side UX convenience with no domain-model or API counterpart expected. Recorded as a formal (low-impact) gap only so this Requirement isn't left unaccounted per fdd-review/CONVENTIONS.md's validation rule, not because it's a substantive finding." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_05_2_5 ;
    sd:impact "L" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "coverage-gap" ;
    rdfs:comment "No notification/task-routing behavior exists off cred:EndorsementDefinitionUpdatedEvent (the closest existing event for 'a new endorsement code was added') to alert the MiEdWorkforce System Admin to define assignment mappings. The 'allowable assignment mappings for Appropriate Placement' being defined is itself a Staffing-domain concept per this FDD's own Dependencies section (Managing Credential use of Assignment Codes, Feature 12.1) — a business specification not yet converted anywhere in mied-v3. Cross-domain gap: the notification trigger belongs to Credentialing, the mapping being defined belongs to a domain this project hasn't reached yet." ;
    oa:hasTarget cred:Req_05_2_7 ;
    sd:impact "M" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .

cred:Annotation_UnformalizedAdminNarrativeContent a sd:Annotation ;
    oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "out-of-scope" ;
    rdfs:comment "The Business Specifications narrative section describes several further Credential-Admin capabilities that were never split into their own Addendum user stories at all, unlike Features 5.1-5.4: Alternative Test Scores management ('detailed requirements will be provided' — a stub even in the narrative), Online Credentialing Viewing management for out-of-state EPPs, Public Credential Search page administration (-> Business Specs 31.1/31.2, corroborated by Wireframe05_28_Redesign's public-facing counterpart), Credential-related system pages administration, Alerts/Notifications management for Credentialing (explicitly 'using the framework of alerts and notifications, Epic 6.0' -> Communications), Email template management for Credentials (same Epic 6.0 framework -> Communications), document-upload availability toggling and file-queue/API-data-ingestion administration (-> Documents capability), and Question Sets/decision-tree management for credential processes (-> the qset:QuestionSetContext stub already declared in solution.ttl) and Internal Comments group/visibility management (-> cred:ApplicationProcessingNotes, already corroborated once by the FDD 11/16 pilot's Req_16_2_2/Question_InternalCommentVisibility). None of these are modeled as sd:Requirement nodes here: most explicitly name their owning Business Specification already (Communications/Documents/Reporting), making them out-of-scope-by-the-FDD's-own-words rather than Credentialing gaps, and the FDD's own numbering caps at 5.6 with no sub-numbers ever assigned to this content — inventing Requirement IDs the source never gave would overstate this ingestion's precision. Flagged collectively here so this content doesn't silently vanish from the coverage picture; worth revisiting once Communications/Documents/Reporting/Question-Sets get their own FDD-review passes, to confirm each item is actually captured somewhere and not lost between FDDs." ;
    sd:impact "M" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn cred:Fdd05Doc .
